## Propositional Logic

Negation
`not` or `¬`

Conjunction (and)
`and` or `∧`

Disjunction (or)
`or` or `∨`

Implication
`->` or `=>` or `arrow.r.double`

Biconditional (iff)
`<->` or `<=>` or `arrow.l.r.double`

Universal quantifier
`forall`

Existential quantifier
`exists`

Entailment/models
`tack.r.double`

Bottom (contradiction)
`bot`

Top (tautology)
`top`

Logical equivalence
`equiv`

Turnstile (proves)
`tack.r`

QED symbol (end of proof)
`qed` or `square.filled` or `square.stroked`

## turnstile

The turnstile `⊢` means "proves" or "derives" in formal logic.

Context: `Gamma tack.r phi` reads as "from assumptions Gamma, we can prove phi"

In German: "Gamma beweist phi" or "aus Gamma folgt phi"
